N2  -  Background Management of abdominal aortic aneurysm (AAA) requires imaging surveillance to evaluate aneurysm size serially. Natural language processing (NLP) has been previously developed to identify patients with AAA retrospectively. However, there are no prior reported prospective studies using NLP to identify AAA patients in real‐time from radiology reports Methods We developed an NLP algorithm for automatically ascertaining AAA cases from radiology reports. NLP was deployed in the institutional big data infrastructure for near real‐time processing of radiology reports. We iteratively refined the NLP algorithm concepts in 3 successive stages. We then compared information extracted by the AAA‐NLP algorithm with gold‐standard manual review of radiology reports by a physician following standardized criteria Results In each stage of iterative validation, the NLP algorithm was modified based on performance compared with manual review. 120 radiology reports were randomly selected for each stage of iterative validation. A total of 360 reports were reviewed. At each stage, the AAA‐NLP algorithm performance improved (Table) Conclusion Implementation of NLP algorithms for the identification of AAA cases from radiology reports in real‐time had high accuracy. This prospective real‐time NLP identification methodology can generate automated input for clinical decision support systems to assist clinicians managing AAA patients [Formula presented]
