o focus groups, as well as social media's ability to procure personal, unbiased information. Digital ethnography provides immediate access to data on a large, diverse population, obviating the logistics required for focus groups. It presents an opportunity for providers to gain awareness of their patients' perceptions, as well as what information their patients seek, facilitating a more effective patient‐provider relationship. (Table Presented).
