N2  -  The goal of this project is to conduct a pilot study to test the utility of a Natural Language Processing (NLP) clinical messaging tool to improve the reach and the quality (fidelity and competency) of coaches providing behavioral activation (BA) strategies through a mobile mental health app called Personalized Real‐time Intervention for Motivational Enhancement (PRIME). This study will improve the reach of clinicians by using a NLP‐powered messaging tool, which will ensure fidelity to the BA model and clinicians will have access to real‐time clinical information about their patients to guide more targeted treatment (competence). If successful, PRIME could operate as a cost effective tool for clinicians to extend their reach and an accessible treatment for the population of those struggling with depression.
